<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 435 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 435 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of September 5 raised 435 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 343 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 168 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.61 (14.74)	   104.6  (63.5)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.92 (16.95)	    82.8  (85.1)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.85 (17.85)	    73.9  (77.3)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.76 (21.76)	   173.8 (117.4)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,560 to the U.S. dollar on Monday, from 1,561 last week. It closed at 1,613 one year ago.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602056 645456</p>
